{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Look down</b> — ת\"ק in gematria. That is: 'look down' — a journey of ת\"ק years from heaven to earth. And ta'gim on the qof, to say: in the merit of Abraham, who begot at one hundred years." "<b>And bless</b> — three times in the Masorah: this one. And the other: 'and bless Your inheritance.' And the third: 'beginning to bless the house of Your servant.' This is what is expounded in Sifrei: 'and bless Your people Israel' — with sons and daughters. And that is 'beginning to bless the house of Your servant.' 'And the land' — with dew and rain. And that is 'and bless Your inheritance.'" "<b>flowing with milk and honey</b> — and adjacent to it:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The phrase השקיפה (look down) is taken to ascend in gematria to the value 500, written as ת\"ק.", 1 "Resolved 'דין' as 'this one' (דין = 'this') referring to the current occurrence of וברך. The third instance is identified as Judges 17:2, where the phrase is הואיל וברך; here rendered as 'beginning to bless' following the sense of הואיל."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:48.122956281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}